description: Preload rules for the typed window.api bridge
globs: src/preload/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Preload Bridge

- Treat preload as the only bridge between renderer code and Electron/Node privileges.
- Expose capabilities through `window.api` with `contextBridge`; do not leak raw Electron modules into the renderer.
- Keep the `ElectronAPI` interface in sync with the methods exposed below it.
- Prefer typed arguments and return values that match shared contracts from `src/shared/types.ts` when data crosses processes.
- Use `ipcRenderer.invoke` for request/response actions and well-scoped listeners for event streams.
- If you add or rename a bridge method here, update the corresponding IPC handler in `src/main/ipc.ts` and all renderer call sites together.
